hdef jotx TechBlogArticleExample

  type page
  title Building a Modern Web Editor with Tiptap
  icon ⚡
  author Engineering Team
  created 2025-01-01
  tags "tech", "tutorial", "web development", "tiptap"

  def heading "Building a Modern Web Editor with Tiptap"

  def paragraph "Rich text editors are the backbone of modern content creation platforms. In this article, we'll explore how to build a production-ready WYSIWYG editor using Tiptap, a headless editor framework built on ProseMirror."

  def callout "💡 What You'll Learn: Set up Tiptap, create custom extensions, handle file uploads, and implement collaborative editing features."

  def divider

  def heading "Why Tiptap?"
    level 2

  def paragraph "Tiptap stands out in the crowded editor space for several reasons. It's framework-agnostic, highly extensible, and provides a clean API for building custom editing experiences."

  def list
    items """Headless architecture - full control over UI
ProseMirror foundation - battle-tested and performant
Rich extension ecosystem
TypeScript support out of the box
Built-in collaborative editing support"""

  def heading "Getting Started"
    level 2

  def paragraph "First, let's install the necessary packages. We'll use React for this example, but the concepts apply to any framework."

  def code
    language bash
    text npm install @tiptap/react @tiptap/pm @tiptap/starter-kit

  def paragraph "Next, create a basic editor component:"

  def code
    language typescript
    text """import { useEditor, EditorContent } from '@tiptap/react'
import StarterKit from '@tiptap/starter-kit'

export function Editor() {
  const editor = useEditor({
    extensions: [StarterKit],
    content: '<p>Start typing...</p>',
  })

  return <EditorContent editor={editor} />
}"""

  def callout "✅ That's it! You now have a working editor with basic formatting capabilities."
    variant success

  def heading "Creating Custom Extensions"
    level 2

  def paragraph "The real power of Tiptap comes from custom extensions. Let's build a custom node for displaying code snippets with syntax highlighting."

  def code
    language typescript
    text """import { Node } from '@tiptap/core'
import { ReactNodeViewRenderer } from '@tiptap/react'
import CodeBlockComponent from './CodeBlockComponent'

export const CodeBlock = Node.create({
  name: 'codeBlock',
  group: 'block',
  content: 'text*',
  marks: '',
  code: true,

  addAttributes() {
    return {
      language: {
        default: 'javascript',
        parseHTML: element => element.getAttribute('data-language'),
        renderHTML: attributes => ({
          'data-language': attributes.language,
        }),
      },
    }
  },

  parseHTML() {
    return [{ tag: 'pre' }]
  },

  renderHTML({ HTMLAttributes }) {
    return ['pre', HTMLAttributes, ['code', {}, 0]]
  },

  addNodeView() {
    return ReactNodeViewRenderer(CodeBlockComponent)
  },
})"""

  def heading "Handling File Uploads"
    level 2

  def paragraph "Image uploads are a common requirement. Here's how to handle drag-and-drop image uploads with proper error handling."

  def mermaid block_19
    src """sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant Editor
    participant Storage
    participant Server
    
    User->>Editor: Drag & drop image
    Editor->>Editor: Validate file (type, size)
    Editor->>Storage: Upload to storage
    Storage->>Server: Store file
    Server->>Storage: Return URL
    Storage->>Editor: Success + URL
    Editor->>Editor: Insert image node
    Editor->>User: Display image"""

  def code
    language typescript
    text """const handleImageUpload = async (file: File) => {
  // Validate file
  if (!file.type.startsWith('image/')) {
    throw new Error('Invalid file type')
  }
  
  if (file.size > 5 * 1024 * 1024) {
    throw new Error('File too large (max 5MB)')
  }
  
  // Upload to storage
  const formData = new FormData()
  formData.append('file', file)
  
  const response = await fetch('/api/upload', {
    method: 'POST',
    body: formData,
  })
  
  const { url } = await response.json()
  return url
}"""

  def heading "Real-Time Collaboration"
    level 2

  def paragraph "Tiptap supports collaborative editing out of the box using Yjs. Here's a minimal setup for real-time collaboration."

  def code
    language typescript
    text """import { useEditor } from '@tiptap/react'
import Collaboration from '@tiptap/extension-collaboration'
import * as Y from 'yjs'
import { WebrtcProvider } from 'y-webrtc'

const ydoc = new Y.Doc()
const provider = new WebrtcProvider('room-name', ydoc)

const editor = useEditor({
  extensions: [
    StarterKit.configure({
      history: false, // Important: disable history for collab
    }),
    Collaboration.configure({
      document: ydoc,
    }),
  ],
})"""

  def callout "⚠️ Production Tip: WebRTC is great for demos, but use a proper WebSocket server (like y-websocket) for production deployments."
    variant warning

  def heading "Performance Optimization"
    level 2

  def paragraph "For large documents, performance matters. Here are key optimizations:"

  def table block_27
    rows """ |  | 
Lazy loading | High | Load content on scroll
Debounce updates | Medium | Wait 300ms before saving
Virtual scrolling | High | Render only visible nodes
Memoization | Medium | Cache rendered components"""

  def heading "Conclusion"
    level 2

  def paragraph "We've covered the essentials of building a modern editor with Tiptap - from basic setup to advanced features like collaboration and performance optimization. The modular architecture makes it easy to start simple and add complexity as needed."

  def callout "✅ Next Steps: Explore the Tiptap documentation, experiment with custom extensions, and join the community Discord for support."
    variant success

  def divider

